WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.420
Good morning, John, and welcome to a special edition of "Let's Understand the News" 'cause this morning my government shut down.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:12.899
Okay, so, yesterday in America we had a government. Today...a little less so. What does it mean? Is the military still protecting us?

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.299
Who's gonna search my bags at the airport? Why did it happen? How is it even possible? Who is responsible?

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.359
What is in my mouth? It is a hair, there was a hair in my mouth.

00:00:21.359 --> 00:00:23.189
Let's go through it. Here in America

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:28.589
there are two different rooms full of people who make the rules. In order for something to become a law, they have to agree on it.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.409
Also, somewhat importantly, they approve the budget

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.209
which is basically the law that makes it legal for the government to spend money. The budget is given to Congress by the

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.550
President and then it is treated like any other bill,

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:44.309
which is to say: very poorly. Often, that abuse of the budget will take so long that Congress will have to pass a continuing resolution

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.030
because they won't be ready

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:51.660
to put the new budget into effect when the old budget comes out of effect. The continuing resolution basically just said "Let's just do what

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.100
the old budget did for a few more weeks while we get our act together."

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.760
These are generally very easy to pass because they're one

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.980
very small step away from doing absolutely nothing. The problem is that Obamacare, which was passed into law in

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:08.908
2010 and upheld by the Supreme Court, today went into full swing. and the Republicans are not done fighting it. The Republican-led house of

00:01:08.979 --> 00:01:10.689
Representatives voted on the continuing resolution

00:01:10.689 --> 00:01:12.839
with a little thing added that said Obamacare:

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:19.949
not gonna happen for another year. The Democrat-controlled Senate is then like, "no that's not what the continuing resolution is for - it's to keep the

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.979
government from shutting down, not making sweeping changes to the most

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:28.829
significant piece of domestic policy in 50 years. Then the House was like "come on, at least come over and talk to us - we got

00:01:28.829 --> 00:01:33.389
root beer!" and the Senate is like "No, man, holding the government hostage: way not cool!

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:38.579
And I don't even like root beer". And then the House was like, "See everybody? The Senate won't even talk to us!

00:01:38.579 --> 00:01:40.020
They're just too cool for school.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:46.170
They WANT the government to shut down, and who doesn't like root beer?" Interestingly, the health care system is funded separately from all this stuff,

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:50.129
so indeed Obamacare went into effect despite the government shutdown today

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:57.118
[sigh] If you want to learn what Obamacare is about, we just launched a new channel called Healthcare Triage and uploaded a video about that very topic.

00:01:57.119 --> 00:01:59.729
Go watch it now, go watch it later, whatever. Now, the Republicans

00:01:59.729 --> 00:02:01.798
don't actually think that they're going to stop Obamacare.

00:02:01.799 --> 00:02:05.578
Which is weird, right? The deeper problem here is that politicians have, over the years,

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.220
redrawn their district lines so that they are more and more

00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:13.779
Republican, or more and more Democrat. This way it's easier to win any given election. However...it's

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.720
radicalized the district, so that if you want to, like,

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:24.159
represent your Ultra-Republican or Ultra-Democrat district YOU have to be really uncooperative and

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:29.529
TERRIBLE at being Congress. That's sort of the root of the problem here:

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:35.290
not an easy problem to fix. As far as what the government shutdown means: things like museums, and national parks, the EPA,

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:42.129
NASA - those things just close down, basically. But things like defense, transportation security, border patrol, food inspectors,

00:02:43.069 --> 00:02:44.930
uh, emergency readiness - those people are

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:51.280
accepted and they get to go to work today. The Postal Service is self-funded, so that's fine; Social Security and Medicare and Medicaid are all

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:57.250
separate from this, so they continue operating. Starting today, about 800,000 people are out of the job, including a very good friend of mine

00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:00.759
(so I'm kind of mad about that) - until Congress gets its act together. No one knows

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:03.429
how quickly this will be resolved - it could be three days, it could be three weeks.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:09.760
But it WILL be resolved because, I have confidence that Congress wants the country to exist. People will lose pay,

00:03:09.769 --> 00:03:15.158
We probably will lose some great employees to the private sector, and the whole world will laugh at our

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:20.738
inability to complete even the most mundane tasks. It's embarrassing, and stupid, and - to be frank - it's a dangerous game

00:03:20.739 --> 00:03:23.649
we're playing, but we will get through it. John, I'll see you on Friday.

